  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 253 PM EDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nWednesday - Sunday...\n\nThe shortwave trough axis will be pushing east of the area by \nWednesday morning, and will close off over the mid Atlantic states \nas we move into late week. Meanwhile, an H5 Omega Block will be \nbuilding from the western Gulf up through the western Great Lakes, \nincluding our area. At the surface, an expansive area of high \npressure over eastern Canada will extend influence into our region. \nThe end result of this pattern will be a period of dry weather from \nmid to late week through the weekend. May need to linger a few small \nrain chances along the I-75 corridor Wednesday morning as the trough \naxis pushes east, otherwise will be dry elsewhere.\n\nIn addition to the dry conditions, temperatures will be notably \ncooler and more comfortable, albeit still around normal for this \ntime of year. Looking for highs mostly in the mid to upper 70s each \nday Wed-Sat, with temps more in the lower 70s for the Bluegrass \nregion. By Sunday, some low 80s will likely return. Dew points will \nsink into the upper 50s and low 60s through mid week, and then down \nmore into the low and mid 50s for the weekend. This will allow for \nsome crisp mornings with lows in the low to mid 50s for the weekend.",
